$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thioethers 8b-f Potassium
carbonate (85 mg, 0.61 mmol, 1.10 equiv.) was added to a solution of
thiol (1.13 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) and stirred for 15 min at room
temperature. A solution of
9-(2’,3’,5’-tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2,6-dichloropurine 3 (250 mg,
0.56 mmol, 1 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) was added and the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at 35°C (HPLC Control). Then the reaction mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (40 mL) and the organic phase was washed with brine (7
× 25 mL), dried over anh. Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc; gradient 33%→66%)
provided product.
9-(2’,3’,5’-Tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-6-dodec-1-ylthio-2-chloro-9H-purine
(8c): a colourless oil. R f = 0.78 (hexane/EtOAc = 1:2). IR (KBr): 2925,
2854, 1755, 1748, 1566, 1439, 1371, 1336, 1232, 1149, 1096, 1048; 1H-NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 8.09 (s, 1H, H-C(8)), 6.18 (d, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' =
5.5 Hz, H-C(1’)), 5.78 (t, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, H-C(2’)),
5.58 (dd, 1H, 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, 3 J 3'-4' = 4.1 Hz, H-C(3’)), 4.42 (dt,
1H, 3 J 3'-4' = 3 J 4'-5b' = 4.1 Hz, 3 J 4'-5a' = 3.2 Hz, H-C(4’)), 4.38
(dd, 1H, 3 J 4'-5a' = 3.2 Hz, 2 J 5a'-5b' = 12.4 Hz, Ha-C(5’)), 4.35 (dd,
1H, 3 J 4'-5b' = 4.1 Hz, 2 J 5a'-5b' = 12.4 Hz, Hb-C(5’)), 3.34 (t, 2H, 3
J = 7.2 Hz, (-CH2-)), 2.13, 2.12, 2.06 (3s, 9H, H3COOC-C(2’,3’,5’)), 1.75
(quintet, 2H, 3 J = 7.2 Hz, (-CH2-)), 1.45 (quintet, 2H, 3 J = 7.2 Hz,
(-CH2-)), 1.34-1.22 (m, 16H, 8(-CH2-)), 0.85 (t, 3H, 3 J = 7.2 Hz,
(-CH3)); 13C-NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 170.2, 169.5, 169.3, 164.5,
153.9, 149.2, 140.8, 130.6, 85.9, 80.5, 73.1, 70.5, 62.9, 31.8, 29.6,
29.5, 29.4, 29.3, 29.2, 29.1, 29.0, 28.9, 28.6, 22.6, 20.7, 20.5, 20.3,
14.0; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C28H42N4O7ClS [M+H]+, 613.2457; found
613.2456.
