$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Synthesis of Compounds 2 Equimolar amounts of the
benzenethiol (2.200 g, 20 mmol) and potassium hydroxide (1.122 g, 20
mmol) were dissolved in dimethyl sulfoxide (25 mL). After dissolution of
the reactants, a solution of 2-chloro-3-quinilinecarboxaldehyde 1 was
added to the mixture. The resulting solution was heated for 6 h
(85-90°C). The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, then
poured into water. A pale-yellow precipitate appeared, which was
filtered, washed with H2O and dried. The crude compound was then
recrystallized in a solution of DMF/ ethanol.
2-Phenylthio-3-quinilinecarboxaldehyde (2a) Yellow solid, yield: 88%. mp
123-124°C; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.58 (s, 1H, -CHO), 8.24 (s, 1H,
quinolin-H4), 8.10-7.19 (m, 9H, Ar-H); IR (KBr) ν: 1705 (C=O), 1626,
(C=N), 762 (C-S-C) cm-1; MS (EI): m/z 265 (M+); Anal. Calcd for
C16H11NOS: C, 72.43; H, 4.18; N, 5.28; Found: C, 72.43; H, 4.22; N, 5.26.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of novel β-lactam-fused 1,5-benzothiazepine derivatives bearing
quinoline moiety
